<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs end mostly firmer, Dow gains sharply.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs end mostly firmer, Dow gains sharply.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs ended mostly firmer in New York on Friday while the Dow Industrials gained 52.90 points to 5,659.86.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company		    Exchange Last	  Net change</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.     US$14 3/4	 +0 1/4</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.     US$22 5/8	 -0 1/4</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.     US$24 1/8	 +0 3/8</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.     US$18 7/8	 -0 3/8</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.     US$13 1/2	 +0 1/8</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.     US$76 1/8	 +0 5/8</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London   34		    nil</p>
<p>Brierley	 London   untraded</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London   231		   nil</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col London   155 1/2	     -1</p>
<p>Templeton	London   135		   -1</p>
<p>Lion	    Sydney   A$3.31		+1</p>
<p>Goodman	 Sydney   A$1.29		nil</p>
<p>Macraes	 Sydney   A$3.20		-4</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
